; S = k·ln(W): entropy arises from the count of microstates (vrnda-sankhya)
; more microstates → more disorder → higher entropy
; entropy IS inverse compression: maximum entropy = minimum compressibility
; a maximally compressed string has zero entropy (one arrangement)
; a random string has maximum entropy (all arrangements equally likely)
; the thermodynamic kramanusara: dS/dT — entropy change wrt temperature
; apeksha is ushna (temperature), NOT thaalam (time)
; Clausius: dS = dQ/T at constant temperature
; entropy's definition S = k·ln(W) is atemporal: kaala is not in the formula
; kaala gives the DIRECTION of entropy change (second law: dS/dt ≥ 0)
; but entropy itself does not have kaala as apeksha — see thermodynamics-varga

(kosha entropy
  (vishesa thermodynamics-varga)
  (swarupa subanta irreversibility kaala-rahita)
  (abheda disorder)
  (sthita kshaya)
  (siddha second-law)
  (janya vrnda-sankhya)
  (pratipaksha sankshepa)
  (kramanusara ushna-apeksha))
